## F-T43-2 (LOW, process) — the M0 guards' self-tests gate nothing today

`.github/workflows/nirmana-m0-guards.yml` is the only CI caller of
`check_asset_catalogue_contract.py --self-test` and `check_asset_source_parity.py
--self-test`. It (a) carries `continue-on-error: true` on both jobs — deliberately, and
that decision is not questioned here — and (b) triggers only on `push`/`pull_request`
against `main` plus `workflow_dispatch`, with `campaign/nirmana-autonomous` deliberately
excluded from `push.branches` to avoid the documented duplicate-trigger problem.

The consequence, which is a real one and I do not think it was intended: **on the campaign
branch, where all of this machinery is being built, those self-tests do not run at all** —
not non-blocking, not at all. Every mutation proof recorded in the M0 reports was a
transcript, and nothing would have re-run it.

M0-T43 does not change that switch (`.github/` is ADHIKĀRIN's, and I was instructed not to
wire anything blocking). What it does instead is call `--self-test` from the ordinary
vitest suite, which does run on every branch and is blocking. That is a workaround for the
symptom; the trigger/branch question is still open and is named here so it is not lost.

